<title>USA: U.S. Mar durable goods orders fell 3.0 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Mar durable goods orders fell 3.0 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Mar     Feb--Rev from     Jan</p>
<p>  New Orders		 -3.0     0.8     1.5	 3.8</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  -4.3    -7.3    -4.1	 1.5</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.    -2.6     3.4     3.1	 4.6</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	-2.6     1.3     1.6	 5.2</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders    -16.8   -12.4    -2.6     -23.0</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders  -4.4     2.3     3.5	 4.4</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   -2.6     7.2     6.9	 3.1</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Mar	Feb---Rev from     Jan</p>
<p> New Orders		171.49   176.81   177.93    175.37</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  37.54    39.21    40.55     42.28</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   133.96   137.60   137.49    133.09</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     166.98   171.38   171.88    169.17</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	4.52     5.43     6.04	6.20</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  44.81    46.87    47.44     45.82</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   39.52    40.59    40.48     37.87</p>
<p>    PERCENT CHANGES:	Mar     Feb--Rev from     Jan</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    0.7     1.9     1.6	 0.9</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders   -0.7     0.6     1.0	 1.0</p>
<p>    BILLIONS OF DLRS:    Mar	Feb---Rev from     Jan</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 174.90   173.63   173.08    170.31</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   493.75   497.15   498.81    493.97</p>
<p> NEW ORDERS-PCT CHANGES   Mar     Feb--Rev from     Jan</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	   -0.6    -0.7    -0.4	 5.1</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery   -1.2     2.1     1.9	 0.9</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery   -5.9     7.7     7.1	17.8</p>
<p>NEW ORDERS-BILLIONS OF DLRS:</p>
<p>  Primary Metals	  15.68    15.78   15.83     15.89</p>
<p>  Industrial Machinery  32.78    33.17   33.13     32.50</p>
<p>  Electrical Machinery  28.81    30.61   30.44     28.42</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected March durable goods orders to be unchanged. Excluding defense orders, they expected a 0.1 percent drop.</p>
<p>The 3.0 percent drop in March total durable goods orders was the largest since a 3.6 percent decline in August 1996, the department said.</p>
<p>The 2.6 percent drop in March durable goods orders excluding transportation was the largest since a 3.0 percent decrease in June 1991, it said.  </p>
<p>A drop in orders for aircraft and parts and motor vehicles and parts contributed to the 4.3 percent decline in March transportation equipment orders, the department said.</p>
<p>It said the 0.7 percent drop in March unfilled orders was the first decline since August 1996.</p>
